		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Closing the FPL Gap & Our GW36 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Hail Cheaters! GW35 offered a raft of differential transfers and captains, showing FPL managers the way forward for closing gaps in a mini league or on overall rank. Brentford look like they're the pick of the bunch, as the form team with the most lopsided matchup in GW36, but who else stood out this weekend? Plus, we ponder just how completely cooked (on a scale of "well done" to "burnt") Liverpool are as fantasy options after clinching the Premier League title. Join us as we set up our teams for GW36 and target the good, the bad, and the beach teams.</p><p>Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/live/GsoTXkq5ehc" target="_blank">https://www.youtube.com/live/GsoTXkq5ehc</a></p><p>Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating" target="_blank">https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating</a></p><p>#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW35 #GW36 #MFFA #hailcheaters</p>
]]></description>
