		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Big Blanks, Free Hits, and Our GW34 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Hail Cheaters! The FPL doubles of GW33 are still in full swing, but thus far it's been a story of single game-weekers—the likes of Mbeumo, Bowen, and Cunha. Ollie Watkins was, admittedly, a surprise hero against Newcastle, and fantasy investors will be hoping for another start midweek at the Etihad. Then it's all eyes on GW34 and the tricky blank fixtures for Arsenal, Aston Villa, Crystal Palace, and Manchester City. With Josh navigating the deadline with just two free transfers, and Brandon unleashing his Free Hit, it's two different strategies that should inform managers in any position. Join us as we zero in on key transfers, Free Hit must-haves, and chalk vs. differential captain picks. </p><p>Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/live/uGv0EaybtLw" target="_blank">https://www.youtube.com/live/uGv0EaybtLw</a></p><p>Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating" target="_blank">https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating</a></p><p>#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW33 #GW34 #MFFA #hailcheaters</p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/Big-Blanks--Free-Hits--and-Our-GW34-Preview-e347ad8</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">e3d3f829-c435-4f7e-b8fd-00d70060bb6a</guid>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[Always Cheating Media LLC]]></dc:creator>
