		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[The FPL Double & Blank Road Ahead: Our GW30 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>After a long break between deadlines, GW30 is finally here. Josh and Brandon run through the International Break news, but more importantly review how this weekend's FA Cup quarterfinal results impact the fantasy schedule for the home stretch. We're getting closer to understanding precisely where the key blanks and doubles will land, so now it's the business of optimizing out FPL squads and how our remaining chips will be activated. (Crystal Palace are now exploding to the front of every manager's mind.) Injury doubts for players like Haaland, Palmer, and Wood add another layer of complexity, so let's get stuck in with this week's episode. Hail Cheaters! </p><p>Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/live/OrWL06F6v9M" target="_blank">https://www.youtube.com/live/OrWL06F6v9M</a></p><p>Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating" target="_blank">https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating</a></p><p>#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW29 #GW30 #MFFA #hailcheaters</p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/The-FPL-Double--Blank-Road-Ahead-Our-GW30-Preview-e347ad3</link>
