		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[FA Cup Fantasy Takeaways & Our GW21 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Join Josh and Brandon as we review the weekend's FA Cup action and unpack relevant FPL takeaways for Tuesday's GW21 deadline. Of course we hit upon the Arsenal vs Man United thriller, Graham Potter's debut as West Ham manager, and the continued march of an in-form Newcastle. Exactly what are we to make of Ruben Amorim's side ahead of a plum Southampton fixture? And are the wheels about to fall off our Arsenal fantasy assets? Plus, we discuss our own GW21 transfer plans and how we rate the tricky captaincy options with Salah about the face a tough defensive challenge. Hail Cheaters!</p><p>Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/live/BDEMZs2nltQ">https://www.youtube.com/live/BDEMZs2nltQ</a></p><p>As mentioned on the pod, we are horrified by the catastrophic scenes in Los Angeles, California. Our hearts go out to everyone affected by the wildfires—and we know that includes many of our cherished listeners and Patreon supporters. If you're looking for a place to send aid, here is a list of businesses, schools, and neighbors that/who are in need: <a href="https://sites.google.com/view/denacommunityrelief/go-fund-me">https://sites.google.com/view/denacommunityrelief/go-fund-me</a></p><p>Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating">https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating</a></p><p>#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW20 #GW21 #MFFA #hailcheaters</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/FA-Cup-Fantasy-Takeaways--Our-GW21-Preview-e347aac</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">6221598e-d15e-11ef-93a5-efdd2b267c27</guid>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[Always Cheating Media LLC]]></dc:creator>
			<pubDate>Mon, 13 Jan 2025 03:33:38 GMT</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://anchor.fm/s/10622ff04/podcast/play/104097548/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2025-5-13%2F402121422-44100-2-30ba6c41005b5130.mp3" length="53118173" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<itunes:summary>&lt;p&gt;Join Josh and Brandon as we review the weekend&apos;s FA Cup action and unpack relevant FPL takeaways for Tuesday&apos;s GW21 deadline. Of course we hit upon the Arsenal vs Man United thriller, Graham Potter&apos;s debut as West Ham manager, and the continued march of an in-form Newcastle. Exactly what are we to make of Ruben Amorim&apos;s side ahead of a plum Southampton fixture? And are the wheels about to fall off our Arsenal fantasy assets? Plus, we discuss our own GW21 transfer plans and how we rate the tricky captaincy options with Salah about the face a tough defensive challenge. Hail Cheaters!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/live/BDEMZs2nltQ&quot;&gt;https://www.youtube.com/live/BDEMZs2nltQ&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;As mentioned on the pod, we are horrified by the catastrophic scenes in Los Angeles, California. Our hearts go out to everyone affected by the wildfires—and we know that includes many of our cherished listeners and Patreon supporters. If you&apos;re looking for a place to send aid, here is a list of businesses, schools, and neighbors that/who are in need: &lt;a href=&quot;https://sites.google.com/view/denacommunityrelief/go-fund-me&quot;&gt;https://sites.google.com/view/denacommunityrelief/go-fund-me&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating&quot;&gt;https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW20 #GW21 #MFFA #hailcheaters&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn more about your ad choices. Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices&quot;&gt;podcastchoices.com/adchoices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
