		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[FPL Strategy for the GW12–16 Fixture Run & Our GW12 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Join Josh and Brandon as we catch up on International Break news including fitness and minutes played for key Fantasy Premier League assets. Who played? Who faked an injury or who had a real one? And what's the outlook for the upcoming GW12? We dig into the fixtures for both this coming weekend and the next five game-weeks for a look at which clubs have the best and worst runs. Arsenal and Chelsea have previously been highlighted as having major swings in difficulty, but how good are their runs really? Maybe it's Bournemouth who are suddenly flying under-the-radar. Plus, there's plenty of Haaland talk and speculation on Saka, Palmer, and the new Manchester United regime. Hail Cheaters!</p><p>Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/live/VDWg0K4GO_A">https://www.youtube.com/live/VDWg0K4GO_A</a></p><p>Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating">https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating</a></p><p>#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW12 #MFFA #hailcheaters</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
