		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Saka's Revenge & Our Kings of the Gameweek Special (GW1–7)]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Join hosts Josh and Brandon as we break down the Premier League and fantasy results from this weekend's GW6. Wildcarders held the narrative during the transfer window, but Cole Palmer takes all the headlines with an incredible four-goal performance against an abject Brighton. So how are FPL managers meant to react? Is Palmer a required premium asset going forward? Or can we keep taking his bursts of points on the chin? Haaland, Salah, and Saka could all hang in the balance. Plus we look ahead to GW7 with key transfer targets and captaincy favorites. Hail Cheaters!</p><p>Watch this episode unfold in video format on our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnEv_LjtGsk">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MnEv_LjtGsk</a></p><p>Support the Cheaters and get exclusive ad-free FPL content: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating">https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating</a></p><p>#bluewirevideo #FPL #PL #GW7 #MFFA #hailcheaters</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
