		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[FPL Buy, Sell, Hold for the Festive Fixtures & Our GW17 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Erling Haaland's absence from Manchester City's GW16 team sheet set off a chain reaction that impacted both our fantasy scores and our core strategy for the upcoming run of festive fixtures. The Norwegian forward is one of many long-held players we now might consider selling. To help fantasy managers reset, Josh and Brandon use this week's episode to evaluate all of the big assets and debate their value in buying, holding, or selling: With Trippier's suspension (and horrid form), does he need to go? Son is hitting a profitable scoring patch, but what does his upcoming Asia Cup duty mean for his value? Are they ANY defenders worth buying? And are form teams like Fulham and Everton suddenly worth a sniff for cheap alternatives? Plus, we look ahead to key transfers and captains for GW17. Hail Cheaters!</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/FPL-Buy--Sell--Hold-for-the-Festive-Fixtures--Our-GW17-Preview-e347agm</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">98241dc2-97e5-11ee-90d6-1b85b02b939d</guid>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[Always Cheating Media LLC]]></dc:creator>
			<pubDate>Mon, 11 Dec 2023 05:29:05 GMT</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://anchor.fm/s/10622ff04/podcast/play/104097750/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2025-5-13%2F402121605-44100-2-b62e2b8e8750133a.mp3" length="66301241" type="audio/mpeg"/>
