		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[UK Here We Come & Making Fantasy Fun Again In GW12]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>This weekend produced a brutal run of results for fantasy managers, resulting in a low-scoring GW11 and a continuation of one of the toughest seasons in memory. Josh and Brandon look to bounce back with their upcoming trip to the U.K. and a GW12 filled with fixtures that will hopefully be easier to predict. Maybe? On this episode we discuss Arsenal's form and injury crisis, as well as Darwin's double personality, Doku's sudden emergence, and Watkins' mysterious track record.</p><p>If you're in the London area, please join us for a listener meet-and-greet this Friday, November 10, at <a href="https://belushis.com/london-bridge">The Dugout at Belushi's London Bridge</a> starting at 7:00 PM. No ticket required, 18+ venue, cash bar. Hope to see you there!</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/UK-Here-We-Come--Making-Fantasy-Fun-Again-In-GW12-e347a6b</link>
