		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Planning for the Big GW10 Fantasy Fixture Shift]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>FPL managers looking for a lifeline this season could see their fortunes change with a notable GW10 fixture swing. Teams like West Ham, Brighton, and Arsenal will finally see some green in the FDR, while Spurs, Chelsea, and even the mighty Manchester City are in for a rough patch. In this week’s episode, we discuss how the upcoming Premier League schedule could impact active wildcards. Plus we weigh the urgency of bringing in both in-form players Mo Salah and Ollie Watkins—and if it’s reasonable to sacrifice Erling Haaland in the process. Hail Cheaters!</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/Planning-for-the-Big-GW10-Fantasy-Fixture-Shift-e347aqi</link>
