		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[FPL Templates, Little-Big At the Back, and Captain Haaland's Expected Minutes]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Special guest <a href="https://twitter.com/_fantasyED">Ed Gray</a> joins us this week to preview the midweek fixtures in GW5 and get set for the FPL deadline. We tackle the current dilemma with Mo Salah—a fantasy phenom who is struggling at the moment to justify his hefty price. Is the Egyptian the first to go if managers are looking to bust the template picks? Plus, we consider our defensive strategies with "big at the back" versus "little-big at the back" where cheaper might actually be better. The captaincy discussion revolves around Erling Haaland, but with the Champions League kicking off in one week, the debate is how strictly the Nordic striker's minutes will be managed. Hail Cheaters!</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/FPL-Templates--Little-Big-At-the-Back--and-Captain-Haalands-Expected-Minutes-e347a7b</link>
