		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Rapid-Fire GW20 Preview]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Boxing Day delivered on exciting football and high-flying Free Hit squads, but also presented more of the same challenges for FPL managers with match postponements and unpredictable lineups. Alas, there's not much time to dwell as the festive fixtures continue on with the midweek round of GW20. Arsenal-Wolves and Aston Villa-Leeds are already off the menu, so in this episode Josh and Brandon are zeroing in on team and player priorities to get us through January. Are Spurs assets about to replace the diminishing fantasy returns of Chelsea? How big a priority is Manchester United at the moment? Plus, we rank our captaincy picks and discuss our own plans. Hail Cheaters!</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/Rapid-Fire-GW20-Preview-e347a5k</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">a2a4b43e-66cb-11ec-9a40-1bc9965e0fcb</guid>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[Always Cheating Media LLC]]></dc:creator>
			<pubDate>Mon, 27 Dec 2021 04:28:53 GMT</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://anchor.fm/s/10622ff04/podcast/play/104097396/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2025-5-13%2F402121166-44100-2-4e382c2ceda6a34c.mp3" length="57493563" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<itunes:summary>&lt;p&gt;Boxing Day delivered on exciting football and high-flying Free Hit squads, but also presented more of the same challenges for FPL managers with match postponements and unpredictable lineups. Alas, there&apos;s not much time to dwell as the festive fixtures continue on with the midweek round of GW20. Arsenal-Wolves and Aston Villa-Leeds are already off the menu, so in this episode Josh and Brandon are zeroing in on team and player priorities to get us through January. Are Spurs assets about to replace the diminishing fantasy returns of Chelsea? How big a priority is Manchester United at the moment? Plus, we rank our captaincy picks and discuss our own plans. Hail Cheaters!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn more about your ad choices. Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices&quot;&gt;podcastchoices.com/adchoices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</itunes:summary>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<itunes:duration>00:59:41</itunes:duration>
			<itunes:image href="https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_episode/43879241/19655ebd15bba82c.jpg"/>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Mid-Season Review: Taking Stock of All 20 Premier League Teams]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>With nearly half the season now behind us, Always Cheating proudly presents our annual mid-season review of all twenty Premier League clubs. Yep, that's Arsenal to Wolves, and everyone in between. We discuss both FPL and real-life player and team performances—best and worst—and how those assessments might influence our fantasy decisions down the home stretch. We also rate clubs on the all-important Make Fantasy Fun Again (xMFFA) scale. Hail Cheaters!</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
