		</item>
		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[10 Things We Think We Think Ahead of GW3]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>So early into a new FPL season, it's very difficult to say what any of us know for sure. What we can identify, though, are things that we think—or at least <em>think</em> we think—about certain clubs, players, and fantasy strategies. This week, we're debating the options among cheap defenders and Tsimikas replacements. We also wax lyrical about Chelsea's deep squad and the awe-inducing reintroduction of Romelu Lukaku to the Premier League. How quickly will we be ripping up our teams to squeeze the Belgian striker in? Plus, we break down Manchester City's predictable hammering of Norwich City, the renewed influence of home supporters on numerous recent results, and the curious choice of an FPL captain ahead of GW3. Hail Cheaters!</p><p>Receive a 25% discount on your Fantasy Football Hub membership: <a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always/">fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always</a></p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/10-Things-We-Think-We-Think-Ahead-of-GW3-e347ahe</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">ccea77ae-03cc-11ec-ae40-db5a6b5125b1</guid>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[Always Cheating Media LLC]]></dc:creator>
			<pubDate>Mon, 23 Aug 2021 04:46:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://anchor.fm/s/10622ff04/podcast/play/104097774/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2025-5-13%2F402121544-44100-2-c7d937e74740651d.mp3" length="72439603" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<itunes:summary>&lt;p&gt;So early into a new FPL season, it&apos;s very difficult to say what any of us know for sure. What we can identify, though, are things that we think—or at least &lt;em&gt;think&lt;/em&gt; we think—about certain clubs, players, and fantasy strategies. This week, we&apos;re debating the options among cheap defenders and Tsimikas replacements. We also wax lyrical about Chelsea&apos;s deep squad and the awe-inducing reintroduction of Romelu Lukaku to the Premier League. How quickly will we be ripping up our teams to squeeze the Belgian striker in? Plus, we break down Manchester City&apos;s predictable hammering of Norwich City, the renewed influence of home supporters on numerous recent results, and the curious choice of an FPL captain ahead of GW3. Hail Cheaters!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Receive a 25% discount on your Fantasy Football Hub membership: &lt;a href=&quot;https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always/&quot;&gt;fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn more about your ad choices. Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices&quot;&gt;podcastchoices.com/adchoices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</itunes:summary>
			<itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
			<itunes:duration>01:15:02</itunes:duration>
			<itunes:image href="https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_episode/43879241/92a7fe63b7fac7e1.jpg"/>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[FPL GW2 Preview: Overperformers, Underperformers, and Head-Scratchers]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>This season's opening fantasy gameweek saw some standout performances and big scores, especially from popular picks Mohamed Salah and Bruno Fernandes. What does this mean for those maverick FPL managers who attempted to go against the grain? Looking ahead to our GW2 squad selections and captaincy picks, we review last weekend's notable over-performers, under-performers, and players and clubs that simply left us scratching our heads. Were Aston Villa and Arsenal really that bad? Were Spurs and Everton really that good? Is it already time to consider dumping Jack Grealish or Ivan Toney? Plus, we debate the bandwagons now building around Paul Pogba, Saïd Benrahma, and Watford stars Ismaïla Sarr and Emmanuel Dennis. Hail Cheaters!</p><p>Receive a 25% discount on your Fantasy Football Hub membership: <a href="https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always/">fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always</a></p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>
]]></description>
			<link>https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/alwayscheating/episodes/FPL-GW2-Preview-Overperformers--Underperformers--and-Head-Scratchers-e347afn</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">0827a6da-fe59-11eb-b825-b302ce644b0b</guid>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[Always Cheating Media LLC]]></dc:creator>
			<pubDate>Mon, 16 Aug 2021 06:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://anchor.fm/s/10622ff04/podcast/play/104097719/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2025-5-13%2F402121529-44100-2-88de287378e4294e.mp3" length="75280900" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<itunes:summary>&lt;p&gt;This season&apos;s opening fantasy gameweek saw some standout performances and big scores, especially from popular picks Mohamed Salah and Bruno Fernandes. What does this mean for those maverick FPL managers who attempted to go against the grain? Looking ahead to our GW2 squad selections and captaincy picks, we review last weekend&apos;s notable over-performers, under-performers, and players and clubs that simply left us scratching our heads. Were Aston Villa and Arsenal really that bad? Were Spurs and Everton really that good? Is it already time to consider dumping Jack Grealish or Ivan Toney? Plus, we debate the bandwagons now building around Paul Pogba, Saïd Benrahma, and Watford stars Ismaïla Sarr and Emmanuel Dennis. Hail Cheaters!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Receive a 25% discount on your Fantasy Football Hub membership: &lt;a href=&quot;https://fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always/&quot;&gt;fantasyfootballhub.co.uk/always&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Learn more about your ad choices. Visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices&quot;&gt;podcastchoices.com/adchoices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
