			<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jun 2020 06:01:39 GMT</pubDate>
			<enclosure url="https://anchor.fm/s/10622ff04/podcast/play/104097658/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2025-5-13%2F402121400-44100-2-cebcfc8359e18fa5.mp3" length="74184513" type="audio/mpeg"/>
			<itunes:summary>&lt;p&gt;The Premier League is returning to action on June 17, and it&apos;s also been confirmed that FPL is along for the ride! To help get us back into the fantasy mindset, this week we&apos;re asking ten unique questions about what we can expect from a rebooted season: How do the opening fixtures look and what are the implications of a double game-week kicking things off? Have we given more thought to the prospect of a round of unlimited transfers? And will line-up rotation and five in-game substitutions upset the norms of building a reliable fantasy squad? We discuss these issues and more and look at what our recent experiences with Fantasy Bundesliga have taught us fantasy in an uncertain era. Hail Cheaters!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Presented by &lt;a href=&quot;https://betonline.ag&quot;&gt;BetOnline.ag&lt;/a&gt;. Set up an account today and use promo code BLUEWIRE for a welcome bonus.&lt;/p&gt;
