		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[FIFA 2019 Women's World Cup: A Primer]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Excitement reigns as the FIFA 2019 Women's World Cup kicks off in France this Friday, June 7. For a preview of the action, we're joined by Jeff Kassouf, author of the new book The Making of the Women's World Cup and founder of https://equalizersoccer.com. Our conversation runs from tournament favorites and dark horses to the general state of play with women's football around the world. Jeff also fill us in on specific players to watch and which match this weekend might be a great place to start for fans who are new to the women's game. Hail Cheaters!<br />
For more information on Jeff Kassouf's new book:<br />
Amazon U.S. - https://www.amazon.com/Making-Womens-World-Cup-Defining/dp/1472143329/ref=sr_1_5<br />
