		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Ep 105: Big Fish (GW16-18)]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>While the big players at Chelsea struggled in GW16, Harry Kane finally delivered on a captaincy for many FPL managers. Always Cheating hosts Josh and Brandon review those and other key takeaways from the weekend as we quickly head into GW17. From defense to strikers, the burning questions in this episode revolve, for the most part, around budget players who we can use to plug holes: Quick-fix, nailed-on cheap defender? Replacing an injured Ramsey with Shaqiri? Choosing between Austin, Mounie, and Calvert-Lewin? There's a lot to consider with these midweek fixtures and then GW18 immediately following at the weekend. Good luck and Hail Cheaters!<br />
