		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Ep 102: Personal Kane-guish (GW12-13)]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>The Premier League returned from its most recent international break with a massive GW12 filled with goals, clean sheets, and a single dark cloud in the shape of Harry Kane. In this episode, we're looking at the Spurs lineup in the aftermath of their loss to Arsenal, compounded by a frustrating run of FPL results for their star striker. We also discuss the awaited and long-awaited returns of Pogba and Ibra, Chelsea's scintillating team display at the Hawthorns, and, when it comes to mid-priced stars like Richarlison and Groß, what "essential" might really mean for FPL managers. Plus, we answer your listener questions before detailing GW13 transfer targets and captain picks. Hail Cheaters!<br />
Become a Patreon supporter: https://www.patreon.com/alwayscheating<br />
