		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Ep 98: President of the World (GW9-10)]]></title>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Manchester City giveth, and then they taketh away. This week we discuss Pep Guardiola's painful yet entirely predictable player rotation. And we're obliged to talk about Harry Kane's big #GW9 Wembley performance, right? Or the lack of any performance whatsoever from Manchester United? Then, for something completely different, we review top performing budget picks (£7.5M and under for midfielders and forwards, £5.0M and under for defenders) through the first quarter of the season and who among those picks is best suited for a late October wildcard. Stick around for our preview of #GW10 fixtures, including picks for captains and clean sheets. Hail Cheaters!<br />
