			<itunes:summary>&lt;p&gt;Manchester City giveth, and then they taketh away. This week we discuss Pep Guardiola&apos;s painful yet entirely predictable player rotation. And we&apos;re obliged to talk about Harry Kane&apos;s big #GW9 Wembley performance, right? Or the lack of any performance whatsoever from Manchester United? Then, for something completely different, we review top performing budget picks (£7.5M and under for midfielders and forwards, £5.0M and under for defenders) through the first quarter of the season and who among those picks is best suited for a late October wildcard. Stick around for our preview of #GW10 fixtures, including picks for captains and clean sheets. Hail Cheaters!&lt;br /&gt;
